{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\n  \"A\": \"Research low-risk copy and allocation removal without changing algorithms. Replace read-only graph/vector value parameters with const references, especially in Prim_ST, find_min_key, is_cycle, deep, coresConjunto and buscaSequencial. Leave recursive history ownership for B. Replace create_partitions' linear walk to the last partition with back/pop_back, retaining its LIFO behavior. Move partition payloads where ownership genuinely transfers, reference unchanged spanning vectors, and reserve predictable capacities where beneficial. Measure changes in small groups: reduced copying is a hypothesis, not an established speedup. Preserve all selection conditions, traversal order, global-best updates and output formatting.\",\n  \"B\": \"Research an order-preserving path-search engine. Build tree adjacency once per processed span by visiting spanning edges in their existing order and appending both endpoints; this must reproduce buscaAresta's neighbor order exactly. Replace copied histories and membership scans with one backtracked path and constant-time on-path flags. Maintain color occurrence counts and a distinct-color counter incrementally; compression can avoid allocating proportional to a potentially large K. Preserve ascending start vertices, leaf-only evaluation, first tropical-path termination, strict improvement of contCor, and best-path state across partitions. Do not terminate when a prefix first contains all colors: the reference prints the completed leaf path. Keep empty-span behavior unchanged. Measure adjacency construction and incremental traversal separately before combining them.\",\n  \"C\": \"Research faithful simplification of Prim_ST. First prove and eliminate its redundant cycle machinery: root 0 is selected first; permanent mat_cycle writes require parent[u] > 0, leaving row 0 empty thereafter; during the first iteration each temporary probe contains only one arc. Consequently is_cycle cannot reject a candidate on a valid simple graph. Measure that removal independently. Next replace new_mat copies with immutable graph storage plus an undirected exclusion overlay, and replace included-vertex maps with dense scratch arrays while preserving sequential assignments and sentinel 100 literally. Reuse workspace where safe. Preserve root 0, ascending minimum-key ties, strict key updates, ascending neighbor processing, parent-dependent include checks, oriented span emission and disconnected returns. A deterministic minimum-index frontier exploiting unit edge weights is a secondary, separately validated experiment—not permission to substitute a textbook spanning-tree enumerator.\",\n  \"G\": \"Integrate only actual programs returned by A/B/C, retaining the fastest validated standalone candidate as a fallback. Resolve overlapping representation and signature changes explicitly, particularly A's cycle-copy reduction versus C's cycle elimination and B's graph/path interfaces. Preserve partition LIFO order, child insertion order, spanning-edge orientation, DFS order, strict best-path ties and first-success output. Evaluate promising combinations and ablations within the existing budget; integrated gains are not additive and regressions must be rejected. Use the untouched correctness and timing machinery with fixed compiler, target and permissions. Require semantic justification beyond the four observed cases, and select the measured winner rather than the most elaborate implementation.\",\n  \"analysis\": \"This run concerns Problem A, src/tropical.cpp. The only measured program is the valid baseline: four correctness cases, mean 0.00526475 seconds, samples approximately 5.10–5.56 ms. There is no profiling or candidate evidence. Source-level opportunities are extensive graph/vector copying, repeated partition-tail scans, repeated tree-edge scans and color recounting, and redundant cycle checks inside Prim. The proposed trees separate allocation/copy reduction, deterministic path traversal, and Prim simplification. On the four-core ARM64 target, the short baseline makes thread-launch overhead and measurement variation important; prioritize serial work removal rather than assume parallelism helps. Correctness is tied to the reference's deterministic path selection, not merely the maximum color count. Do not replace it with an arbitrary optimal path, repair unusual enumeration rules as an optimization, or specialize to the measured cases.\"\n}"}}
